Subject: [PATCH] [mlir][affine] Verify that affine.delinearize_index has a result

The generated verifier of affine.delinearize_index reads the type of its
first result to compare it with the linear index's (the TypesMatchWith
that infers the linear index's type when parsing), so an op with an
empty basis and no result, which the builders make, asserted instead of
being reported. Such an op cannot be meant: the custom form cannot spell
it and the folder returns one result for it. Declare that the op has a
result, before the type check, and say so in its description.

---
diff --git a/mlir/include/mlir/Dialect/Affine/IR/AffineOps.td b/mlir/include/mlir/Dialect/Affine/IR/AffineOps.td
index 6215d5c29..8eea8b475 100644
--- a/mlir/include/mlir/Dialect/Affine/IR/AffineOps.td
+++ b/mlir/include/mlir/Dialect/Affine/IR/AffineOps.td
@@ -1109,6 +1109,8 @@ def AffineVectorStoreOp : AffineStoreOpBase<"vector_store"> {
 def AffineDelinearizeIndexOp : Affine_Op<"delinearize_index",
     [Pure, Elementwise,
      DeclareOpInterfaceMethods<InferIntDivisibilityOpInterface>,
+     // Checked before the first result type is read below.
+     PredOpTrait<"has at least one result", CPred<"$_op.getNumResults() != 0">>,
      // Infer linear_index type from the first result type during parsing.
      TypesMatchWith<"linear_index type must match result types",
                     "multi_index", "linear_index", "$_self[0]">
@@ -1138,7 +1140,8 @@ def AffineDelinearizeIndexOp : Affine_Op<"delinearize_index",
     In other words, `%0:3 = affine.delinearize_index %x into (B, C)` produces
     `%0 = {%x / (B * C), (%x mod (B * C)) / C, %x mod C}`.
 
-    The basis may either contain `N` or `N-1` elements, where `N` is the number of results.
+    The basis may either contain `N` or `N-1` elements, where `N` is the number of results,
+    of which there is at least one.
     If there are N basis elements, the first one will not be used during computations,
     but may be used during analysis and canonicalization to eliminate terms from
     the `affine.delinearize_index` or to enable conclusions about the total size of
diff --git a/mlir/test/Dialect/Affine/invalid.mlir b/mlir/test/Dialect/Affine/invalid.mlir
index 3afebfcc0..ceaa41334 100644
--- a/mlir/test/Dialect/Affine/invalid.mlir
+++ b/mlir/test/Dialect/Affine/invalid.mlir
@@ -522,6 +522,14 @@ func.func @delinearize(%idx: index) {
 
 // -----
 
+func.func @delinearize_no_result(%idx: index) {
+  // expected-error@+1 {{'affine.delinearize_index' op failed to verify that has at least one result}}
+  "affine.delinearize_index"(%idx) <{static_basis = array<i64>}> : (index) -> ()
+  return
+}
+
+// -----
+
 func.func @linearize(%idx: index, %basis0: index, %basis1 :index) -> index {
   // expected-error@+1 {{'affine.linearize_index' op should be passed a basis element for each index except possibly the first}}
   %0 = affine.linearize_index [%idx] by (%basis0, %basis1) : index
